{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QBesselContiguityRecurrence"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.binding_sl2_constant_ratio_degeneration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.binding_sl2_constant_ratio_degeneration","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingQBesselKernel.lean#L75-L83","doc":"**Layer 1 as the constant-ratio degeneration of Layer 2.** If instead the binding ratio is a\n*constant* `ρ` (the `q → 1` limit, `ρ = λ₊ = e^{θ_binding}` the SL₂ eigenvalue), the period is\ngeometric `a_D^(n) = a_D^(0)·ρⁿ` — the C-finite depth-2 SL₂ effective fit\n(`BindingHyperbolicRecurrence`). This is the honest statement of \"the SL₂ τ is the `n ≤ 4`\ndegeneration\": same `first_order_solution`, ratio collapsed to a constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.binding_qbessel_second_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.binding_qbessel_second_order","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingQBesselKernel.lean#L65-L73","doc":"**Layer 2 — second-order q-difference equation `(☆)` (conditional).** The same binding\ncoefficients satisfy the function-level q-Bessel q-difference equation's coefficient form,\n`(a q^{2k+1} − q^{k+1} − a q^k + 1)·a_D^(k+1) + q^k·a_D^(k) = 0`, via\n`qbessel_second_order_recurrence`. This is the explicit `q`-difference operator annihilating the\nbinding generating function — the Layer-2 analogue of the depth-2 SL₂ operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.binding_qbessel_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.binding_qbessel_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingQBesselKernel.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**Layer 2 — q-holonomic closed form (conditional on `BindingFollowsQBessel`).** The binding\nperiod is the q-hypergeometric product `a_D^(n) = a_D^(0) · ∏_{j<n} qbesselRatio q a j` — the\nsuper-exponential sequence, derived from the q-Bessel contiguity via `qbessel_coeff_closed_form`.\nThe product of `q^k`-dependent ratios is what produces the factorial `(1/2)_n` growth (PR #2795). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.BindingFollowsQBessel.contiguity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.BindingFollowsQBessel.contiguity","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingQBesselKernel.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The Hahn–Exton q-Bessel contiguity `(★)` for the binding coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.BindingFollowsQBessel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.BindingFollowsQBessel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingQBesselKernel.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.BindingFollowsQBessel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQBesselKernel.BindingFollowsQBessel","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingQBesselKernel.lean#L45-L53","doc":"**The binding prolongation follows the q-Bessel contiguity — `conj` (bean `z2bn`).**\nThe binding generating-function coefficients `aD n = a_D^(n)` satisfy the Hahn–Exton q-Bessel\nfirst-order q-recurrence `(★)`: `aD (k+1)·(1−q^{k+1})(1−a q^k) = −q^k · aD k` (with `a = q^{ν+1}`).\nThis is the §3b conjecture that the super-exponential binding period (= `lw(n−1)`, #1765) is the\nq-holonomic q-Bessel sequence — the fibre q-difference kernel `R(q,x)`. The single conjectural\ninput; the consequences below are derived. ","signatureChunk":0}]}